Q("Custody accounts are distinguished from CIT because:", ["CIT is monthly", "CIT is the business's own cost — custody is other parties' money in transit", "CIT is smaller", "There is no difference"], 1, "The wallet's compartments versus the business's own liabilities.", "Ch1"),
Q("Every custody compartment follows one pattern:", ["Account only", "An account, fed by documents, reconciled to a register, cleared by a remittance routine", "A spreadsheet", "An annual filing"], 1, "One pattern, five appearances.", "Ch1"),
Q("PAYE is remitted to:", ["The federal service", "The state authority of each employee's residence", "The employer's state only", "Any state"], 1, "The federal/state split: VAT and CIT federal; PAYE to states.", "Ch2"),
Q("A working consequence of the 2025 reform is:", ["Paper filing returned", "The invoice register and the filed return increasingly reconcile automatically on the authority's side", "VAT was abolished", "PAYE went federal"], 1, "Register discipline moved from good practice to survival.", "Ch2"),
Q("Tax positions (what qualifies, what rate) belong to:", ["The system", "The accountant and the tax adviser — the machinery is this module's territory", "The auditor", "The MD"], 1, "The competence boundary.", "Ch2"),
